==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|takes the cake|taking the cake|took the cake|taken the cake}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial|US}} To be especially [[good]] or [[outstanding]].
#: ''Thanks! You guys '''take the cake'''.''
#: ''Once the party was over, everyone agreed that Elizabeth and her Harriet Tubman getup had '''taken the cake'''.''
# {{lb|en|colloquial|US}} To be particularly [[bad]], [[objectionable]], or [[egregious]].
#: ''I've seen bad grammar, but this '''takes the cake'''.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to be good or outstanding}} {{l|en|steal the show}}
* {{sense|to be particularly bad or egregious}} {{l|en|take the biscuit}} (''British'')

